== Match report ==

=== Balisca 3–1 Orma ===
Co-hosts [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] secured third place at the [[2026 AFA World Cup]] with a comfortable victory over [[Orma national football team|Orma]] in [[Martapura]].

[[Marc Soler i Vidal]] opened the scoring for Balisca in the 13th minute, giving them an early lead that they held through to half-time. In the second half, Soler i Vidal doubled his tally in the 63rd minute before [[Iker Goikoetxea]] added a third in the 67th to put the match beyond Orma's reach.

[[Mikael Dirra]] pulled one back for Orma in the 71st minute — his fifth goal of the tournament — but it proved to be only a consolation. Balisca held on to claim third place on home soil, salvaging some pride after their semi-final elimination.

== Summary ==

Balisca finished third at the 2026 AFA World Cup, their best result since finishing as runners-up in 2018. Orma's remarkable tournament — which saw them advance from the round of 16 with comeback victories — ended with a fourth-place finish.

